## 12. Research Background

E³ originates from cross-disciplinary exploration across architecture, film, language education, industrial systems, and applied problem-solving.

A recurring observation is that different domains often contain transferable relationships involving goals, dependencies, constraints, incomplete structures, feedback, and preservation.

These experiences motivated a broader research direction:

**Can we identify the structures that make effective reasoning transferable, and train AI systems to discover and use those structures themselves?**

The project approaches this question by combining formal modeling, quantitative evaluation, and experimental agent learning.

---

## 13. Research Status

E³ is currently an open theoretical and methodological research proposal. Its core architecture, mathematical formulations, and experimental directions are being developed for collaborative validation.

The project builds on established work in Transformers, reinforcement learning, information theory, grammar-constrained generation, topology, and decision science. Its proposed contribution is the integration of these methods around Logical State Stack, Cumulative Tension, Protective Value, and decision-sufficient structural learning.

Experimental implementations and independently verified results will be added as the research progresses.

